test('accepts low but valid ZIPs', () => {
  assert.ok(ZIP_RE.test('00501'));
  assert.ok(ZIP_RE.test('10000'));
});

// add to the `bad` array:
'00000', '00000-1234',
```

If you use the stricter pattern, also add `'12345-0000'` to `bad`.

Lookaheads work in every modern JavaScript engine, so you don't need any flags. This is still only a format check, though. `00000` is just the most obvious fake ZIP. Plenty of other well-formed codes like `00001` don't exist either, so if real validity matters, a USPS lookup is still the answer. You're clearly the type to want that eventually, so it's worth planning for.

